                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Overall an intriguing early approach to the genre of psychological memory games. The puzzles were often either too straightforward or mindnumbingly reliant on precise timing and other precise returns to particular memories. While I love a non-linear storyline, this one was a bit too vague at times. While I know this vagueness is central to the premise of this game, it often left me confused as to what I was to do next. I loved the approach to the AI overseer, though.",
